'''Sagat Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] who is unlocked by rolling [[Cat Capsule|Rare Cat Capsules]] during [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 579
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Sagat Cat
|name2 = Sagat Cat CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sagat Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sagat Cat mainly suffers from mediocre stats and single target, even with his ability bolstering his stats against Floating enemies. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Mer-Cat]] entirely outclasses Sagat Cat, even in her first form. She hits harder than Sagat and can be spammed more easily. While Sagat has almost double Mer-Cat's bulk at the same level, he also has nearly double her cooldown. Additionally, Mer-Cat has the Survive ability, meaning that while she has less health, she can survive hits that even Sagat Cat can't.

While his immunity to waves may be useful, he can only really use it if he was spammable enough to be a good anti-wave meatshield or have the stats to do something when surviving longer because of this wave immunity. Unfortunately, because neither applies to Sagat Cat, he is outclassed in his wave-immune niche by [[Talents|Talented]] [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Catley]] just as he is outclassed in his anti-Floating niche by Mer-Cat. Additionally, [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Glittering Gold Cat]] and Talented [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] outclass them both as a wave-immune meatshield.

